  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Niger Community Cohesion Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This program builds upon the lessons learned from two previously implemented phases in the country and on their achievements. This third phase benefits from the network of peace committees, as well as relationships and networks of trust built with local authorities in key areas of the Diffa and Tillab&#xe9;ri regions since the inception of the programme and in Tahoua since mid-2020. This phase ensures the continuity of the flexible and rapid grant mechanism, expanded to areas not yet covered within the scope of the program, in order to support activities and responses addressing the main drivers of conflict and instability, as well as possible displacement in selected areas based on key needs identified by the Nigerien High Authority for Peacebuilding (HACP). While Diffa, Tillab&#xe9;ri, and Tahoua remain the primary locations, activities in border areas may be considered, based on the security situation, availability of funds, the potential impact the program may have on the intervention area, and priorities of the HACP, the European Union, and the International Organization for Migration.</narrative>
  </description>
